{
  "said": "I pull the pads, clean everything up, pop the new ones in, torque the caliper bolts to 7.5 Nm, and then bed them in down the lane with twenty gentle stops. If there's any fork oil or brake fluid on the disc, the bike doesn't go out at all because new pads won't fix a contaminated rotor.",
  "used_facts": [
    "what the job is",
    "caliper bolt torque",
    "bedding in",
    "what stops the job dead"
  ],
  "knew_it": true
}
